    "updated_at": "2023-04-21T21:26:23Z",
    "body": "> * [x]  [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\r\n>   \r\n>   * [Add checks for popovers moving between documents web-platform-tests/wpt#39599](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/39599)\r\n\r\nI can't seem to comment after the issue is merged, so here is my comment:\r\nMy confusion is this, in popover-removal-2.html the expectation is that after moving the popover to a new document the popover will be closed. But in this subtest the hidePopover will fire beforetoggle, the event listener will be called, the popover moved to a new document, which should cause an internal hidePopover (popover removed from document logic), and then the final popover check in hidePopover should check that the popover is in showing state, which it is not anymore (because of popover removed from document logic).\r\nAm I missing something? Is the \"popover removed from document\" logic not triggered in this case?",
