    "updated_at": "2023-04-21T22:34:33Z",
    "body": "> Yeah when the popover is removed from the document while moving it to the other document, then the removal steps which run before the element is actually removed should hide the popover.\r\n> Are you implementing this in WebKit? What's happening? Is the popover still showing when it's moved to the other document?\r\n\r\nYes, implementing here:\r\nhttps://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/13024\r\n\r\nIn WebKit above happens as you describe, i.e. popover removal/move to other document triggers the hidePopover internally during beforetoggle, and after the beforetoggle operation ends the next step will be checking the popover and it will fail because the expectation is that the popover is showing so the hidePopover can do its final steps, but in fact it is not showing anymore, hence the failure in the second subtest. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
