    "updated_at": "2023-04-24T15:17:22Z",
    "body": "For reference, I believe https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#remove-an-element-from-a-document, which has as step 4 hiding the popover, is being used in the appendChild operation in the second subtest, and checking the popover state after the beforetoggle is handled will raise the exception. Regardless if this interpretation is correct, I can't tell why chromium currently does not raise an exception here.",
